<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="container">
    <div class="content-box hero">
        <h1>🎭 Ceremonies & Traditions 🎭</h1>
        <p>Sacred rituals and celebrations of the Circles Dynasty</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Annual Ceremonies</h2>
        
        <div class="ceremony-card">
            <h3>🎊 The Festival of Pi (March 14th)</h3>
            <p><strong>Time:</strong> Celebrated precisely at 1:59 PM (3/14 1:59 - the digits of π)</p>
            <p><strong>Description:</strong> The grandest celebration in the circular calendar! Citizens gather at the Great Round Plaza to honor the sacred ratio. King Circumfero leads the "Circumnavigation Procession," walking the outer boundary of the capital in exactly 2πr steps.</p>
            <p><strong>Traditions:</strong></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
                <li>Baking circular pies and sharing them in sectors</li>
                <li>Reciting digits of π from memory (current record: 70,000 digits by Sage Memorius)</li>
                <li>The Royal Pi Relay - teams pass a circular disc while chanting "three point one four"</li>
                <li>Children draw circles in the sand, competing for perfect roundness</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Royal Proclamation:</strong> On this day, King Circumfero grants one wish to any subject who can prove a new theorem about circles.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card">
            <h3>🌕 The Ceremony of Complete Rotation</h3>
            <p><strong>Time:</strong> Held at midnight on the winter solstice</p>
            <p><strong>Description:</strong> A solemn ceremony marking the completion of one full rotation around the sun. All circles in the realm perform a synchronized 360° rotation, symbolizing the cyclical nature of existence.</p>
            <p><strong>Traditions:</strong></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
                <li>Lighting 360 candles arranged in a perfect circle</li>
                <li>The Royal Family stands at the center while subjects encircle them</li>
                <li>Each attendee completes one full turn, returning to their starting position</li>
                <li>Silent meditation on the perfection of returning to one's origin</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Symbolic Meaning:</strong> "We end where we begin, yet we are transformed by the journey."</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card">
            <h3>💫 The Tangent Touch Ceremony</h3>
            <p><strong>Time:</strong> First day of spring</p>
            <p><strong>Description:</strong> Princess Tangentia presides over this ceremony celebrating connection and boundaries. Couples come from far and wide to receive her blessing, as tangent lines represent the perfect kiss - touching at one point yet respecting boundaries.</p>
            <p><strong>Traditions:</strong></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
                <li>Engaged couples stand in a circle while Princess Tangentia draws a tangent line</li>
                <li>The "Dance of Perpendicularity" - partners move in perfect 90° coordination</li>
                <li>Exchange of circular rings symbolizing eternal commitment</li>
                <li>The blessing: "May you touch hearts at one point, yet extend infinitely together"</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card">
            <h3>👑 The Coronation of Concentricity</h3>
            <p><strong>Time:</strong> Every 100 years</p>
            <p><strong>Description:</strong> When a new circle is admitted to the Sacred Council, they undergo the Coronation of Concentricity. The initiate must prove they share the same center as the royal family.</p>
            <p><strong>Trials:</strong></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
                <li><strong>The Test of Origin:</strong> Finding the exact center point through three chords</li>
                <li><strong>The Trial of Parallel:</strong> Maintaining perfect distance from the throne at all times</li>
                <li><strong>The Challenge of Growth:</strong> Expanding radius without losing the center</li>
                <li><strong>The Vow of Symmetry:</strong> Pledging to maintain rotational balance</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Reward:</strong> A seat on the Sacred Council and the title "Circle of the Realm"</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Life Cycle Ceremonies</h2>
        
        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #4facfe 0%, #00f2fe 100%);">
            <h3>🌱 The Birth Ritual - Drawing of the First Circle</h3>
            <p>When a new circle comes into existence, the Royal Geometer traces their circumference with the Golden Compass. The newborn's radius is measured and recorded in the Book of All Circles.</p>
            <p><strong>Blessing:</strong> "May your center be true, your radius constant, and your circumference eternal."</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #fa709a 0%, #fee140 100%);">
            <h3>🎓 The Rite of Radius - Coming of Age</h3>
            <p>At age 314 (π × 100), young circles undergo the Rite of Radius. They must calculate their own area and circumference without assistance, proving their understanding of their circular nature.</p>
            <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Draw a perfect circle freehand. The closer to perfection, the greater the honor.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #a8c0ff 0%, #3f2b96 100%);">
            <h3>💒 The Unity Circle - Marriage Ceremony</h3>
            <p>Two circles unite by finding a common tangent line, symbolizing two separate entities touching without losing their individual identity. Queen Arealia presides, blessing the union with the words: "Two circles, one love, infinite possibilities."</p>
            <p><strong>Tradition:</strong> The couple creates a Venn diagram, with the overlap representing their shared future.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);">
            <h3>🕊️ The Return to Origin - Memorial Rite</h3>
            <p>When a circle completes their final rotation, they "return to the origin." The community gathers in concentric circles around the departed, spiraling inward until all meet at the center point.</p>
            <p><strong>Eulogy:</strong> "From point to circle, from circle to point. The journey is complete."</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Daily Rituals & Practices</h2>
        
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🌅 Morning Circumambulation</h3>
                <p>Loyal subjects walk in a clockwise circle each morning, greeting the sun with rotational reverence. This practice is believed to align one's personal radius with the cosmic order.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🍽️ The Round Table Dining</h3>
                <p>All meals are served on circular tables where no seat is more important than another. This tradition, started by King Circumfero, ensures democratic discussion and equal voice.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>📿 Meditation of the Center</h3>
                <p>Twice daily, citizens practice "centering" - a meditation focusing on their inner center point, from which all aspects of life radiate equally.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎨 Circular Calligraphy</h3>
                <p>The art of writing in spiral patterns, starting from the center and radiating outward. Master calligraphers can inscribe entire poems in one continuous curve.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Seasonal Celebrations</h2>
        
        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f093fb 0%, #f5576c 100%);">
            <h3>🌸 Spring Equinox - The Blooming of Circles</h3>
            <p>Celebrating new growth and expansion. Circles of all sizes gather to honor nature's circular patterns - from flower petals to tree rings. Garden competitions award the most perfectly circular flower beds.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fad0c4 0%, #ffd1ff 100%);">
            <h3>☀️ Summer Solstice - The Festival of Maximum Radius</h3>
            <p>On the longest day, the dynasty celebrates expansion and growth. Circles are encouraged to increase their radius slightly, symbolizing personal growth and extended influence.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fecfef 100%);">
            <h3>🍂 Autumn Equinox - The Gathering of Concentric Wisdom</h3>
            <p>Elders share their wisdom with younger circles. The Sacred Council meets publicly, demonstrating how concentric circles of different sizes can all share the same truth at their center.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a8edea 0%, #fed6e3 100%);">
            <h3>❄️ Winter Solstice - The Ceremony of Complete Rotation (detailed above)</h3>
            <p>The year's most solemn ceremony, marking completion and new beginning - the perfect circular concept of eternal return.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Special Ceremonial Objects</h2>
        
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>⚱️ The Sacred Compass</h3>
                <p>Used only by the Royal Geometer, this golden compass is said to have drawn the very first circle. Its point never dulls, and its arc is always perfect.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>📜 The Scroll of Circumferences</h3>
                <p>An ancient scroll that rolls into a perfect circle. It contains the names of every circle ever recognized by the dynasty, written in spiral script.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>💎 The Crystal Orb of Symmetry</h3>
                <p>A perfectly spherical crystal that displays circular cross-sections from any angle. Used in ceremonies to demonstrate the principle "As above, so below; as within, so without."</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎺 The Circular Horn</h3>
                <p>Blown to announce royal proclamations, this horn produces a perfect sine wave - the mathematical expression of circular motion through time.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Ceremonial Dress Code</h2>
        <p>For formal ceremonies, specific attire is required:</p>
        <ul style="line-height: 2.5; font-size: 1.1rem;">
            <li>👗 Robes must have circular patterns or be free of corners</li>
            <li>👑 Crowns and tiaras must feature circular gems</li>
            <li>🥾 Ceremonial shoes must leave circular footprints</li>
            <li>💍 All jewelry must be rings, bracelets, or circular pendants</li>
            <li>🎭 Face paint in concentric circles denotes rank within the council</li>
            <li>🔮 The Royal Family wears cloaks that create perfect circular shadows</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Sacred Oaths & Pledges</h2>
        
        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);">
            <h3>The Oath of the Circle Guard</h3>
            <p style="font-style: italic; font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 1rem 0; padding: 1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border-radius: 5px;">
                "I pledge my radius to the realm,<br>
                My circumference to the crown,<br>
                My center to the eternal truth,<br>
                And my rotation to the royal cause.<br>
                As a circle has no end,<br>
                So my loyalty knows no bounds."
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ceremony-card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffecd2 0%, #fcb69f 100%);">
            <h3>The Scholar's Vow</h3>
            <p style="font-style: italic; font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 1rem 0; padding: 1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border-radius: 5px;">
                "I shall seek the center of all knowledge,<br>
                Draw conclusions with perfect circumference,<br>
                Maintain intellectual symmetry in all directions,<br>
                And remember that wisdom, like a circle,<br>
                Encompasses all yet excludes none."
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Festival Calendar</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">The Circles Dynasty follows a circular calendar where the year curves back on itself. Each month is divided into 30 days, and the year contains 12 cycles plus 5 sacred days of rest at the center.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>Sacred Days:</strong> The five days when time itself is said to curve back and touch its beginning, allowing for reflection and renewal before the next rotation begins.</p>
    </div>
</div>

